      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 473,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Macroscopic appearance",
    "headingPosition": 11,
    "headingid": 386,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 64797,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 489,
        "headingId": 386,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>The macroscopic appearance is similar to that of HPV-associated SCC.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-08T17:00:23"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 467,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Histopathology",
    "headingPosition": 12,
    "headingid": 380,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 64798,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 489,
        "headingId": 380,
        "headingText": "<p>The histopathology is similar to that of HPV-associated vaginal SCC. The majority of cases are of the keratinizing type {21166704; 18500261}. p16 negativity and p53 immunopositivity are common findings. Immunostaining with p16 is not entirely reliable {22226684}; 38.9% of HPV-independent tumours were p16-immunopositive in a meta-analysis of vaginal SCCs {30561092}.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2020-08-12T12:14:41"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 468,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Cytology",
    "headingPosition": 13,
    "headingid": 381,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 64799,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 489,
        "headingId": 381,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>HPV-associated and HPV-independent squamous cell carcinomas are indistinguishable on the basis of morphology {30911077}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-08T17:00:23"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 469,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Diagnostic molecular pathology",
    "headingPosition": 14,
    "headingid": 382,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 64800,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 489,
        "headingId": 382,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not clinically relevant</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-08T17:00:23"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 472,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Essential and desirable diagnostic criteria",
    "headingPosition": 15,
    "headingid": 385,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 64801,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 489,
        "headingId": 385,
        "headingText": "<p><em>Essential:</em> no previous (&le;&nbsp;5&nbsp;years) or concomitant SCC of cervix or vulva; infiltrating, angulated, irregularly sized and shaped nests, anastomosing cords, and solid sheets; nuclear pleomorphism and increased mitotic count; a desmoplastic or inflammatory stroma; negative p16 immunostaining with appropriate positive internal control.</p>\r\n<p><em>Desirable:</em> molecular testing for HPV is advisable.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2020-07-21T16:40:06"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 470,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Staging",
    "headingPosition": 16,
    "headingid": 383,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 64802,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 489,
        "headingId": 383,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>The staging is the same as for other vaginal tumours.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-08T17:00:23"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 471,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Prognosis and prediction",
    "headingPosition": 17,
    "headingid": 384,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 64803,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 489,
        "headingId": 384,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Overall and progression-free survival rates are significantly lower with HPV-independent SCC than with HPV-associated tumours {21666483; 2166263; 23402906; 22226684}.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-08T17:00:23"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  }
]